# Naming and File Conventions

## Folders

Use clear responsibility-based folders.
Do not create nested folders that only contain one file unless the structure is expected to grow.

## Type names

Use PascalCase for public TypeScript types and interfaces where appropriate.
Use clear domain names such as `Product`, `QuoteRequest`, `JournalEntry`.

## Variables

Use descriptive camelCase names.
Avoid one-letter variables outside tiny local loops.

## Constants

Use named constants for reusable configuration and content keys.
Do not scatter magic strings throughout templates.

## Sanity fields

Prefer predictable camelCase field names.
Keep front-end mapping explicit when CMS naming differs.

## URL conventions

Use lowercase kebab-case paths.
Examples:
- `/who-we-serve`
- `/request-a-quote`
- `/products/microgreens`

## Environment variables

Use explicit names that indicate server/client exposure intent.
Never expose secrets through public environment prefixes.

## Imports

Prefer project aliases when configured.
Avoid deep relative import chains when a stable alias improves readability.
